➤ What Are SSH Keys🔐?
SSH keys are a pair of cryptographic keys used to securely log into remote systems like servers without needing a password.
→ ssh keys consisting of public and private keys.

1️⃣ Public Key: A cryptographic key that is shared with servers to allow secure communication. It is used to verify the private key.
2️⃣ Private Key: A secret cryptographic key stored securely on your device. It is used to prove your identity and establish a secure connection.

→ When you try to connect: The server checks if your private key matches the public key. If they match, you're allowed in no password needed.

🎯 Why SSH Keys Are Better Than Passwords:
→ More Secure Than Passwords (Hackers can guess or steal passwords but SSH keys are very hard to crack.)
→ Help you connect without typing your password every time.
→ Used by platforms like GitHub, AWS, GCP, Azure, etc.
→ Supports secure file transfers via SFTP and SCP
→ Ideal for scripts, deployments, and CI/CD pipelines enables secure automated logins

➤ Many services (like GitHub and AWS) don’t allow password login for better security they require SSH keys.!
